<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 32,521 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 32,521 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 32,521 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 67,534 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	June 15</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,933	40,261</p>
<p>    Import cargo		20,588	27,273</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ship sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and six are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 Themera		   17/6</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     42,000	 Yasmeen		   17/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		6,000	 Bunga Siantan	   22/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
